02:08.520 --> 02:11.100
Saylor doesn't care. He's back to buying.

02:11.560 --> 02:13.580
And the comments still can't really understand.

02:13.760 --> 02:16.020
They still think they know better, which is always pretty funny.

02:16.260 --> 02:19.860
Accusing him of buying high and selling low really is just this, isn't it?

02:19.900 --> 02:23.260
I did also wake up to see this this morning and this even got me, okay?

02:23.460 --> 02:25.440
This tape slavery caught me out.

02:25.500 --> 02:30.400
And the only reason I wanted to point at this is to try and help out anyone that is very new to markets, okay?

02:30.400 --> 02:42.140
If you are in the habit of seeing posts like this on Twitter, one, either unfollow them or number two, get into the habit of double checking on a daily time frame or a weekly time frame chart.

02:42.200 --> 02:43.380
Because this even got me.

02:43.440 --> 02:46.800
I was like, oh no, my yellow squiggle might be in jeopardy here too.

02:47.180 --> 02:49.220
But this is what we're dealing with, okay?

02:49.260 --> 02:51.520
I can barely even see this daily candle, okay?

02:51.560 --> 02:56.400
So you can massage the charts to make it look hyperbolic for clicks and engagement.

02:56.400 --> 03:03.440
And again, as a sort of public service announcement, if you are newer to markets, then do not allow posts like this to get you.

03:03.640 --> 03:07.440
This even got me, like I said this morning, and that's what they're designed to do at the end of the day.

03:07.500 --> 03:10.980
They are designed to trigger your fight or flight system.

03:11.120 --> 03:15.220
They're designed to create an emotional response so that you do dumb stuff.

03:15.460 --> 03:18.700
Dumb stuff pertaining to your risk management and capital allocation.

03:18.920 --> 03:22.080
But when we zoom out and look at this, okay, we can't even see this daily candle.

03:22.460 --> 03:23.820
So we don't have to worry about it.

03:23.820 --> 03:26.760
So do get in the habit of double checking on a zoomed out chart.

03:26.900 --> 03:35.820
Honestly, you will thrive if you get into the habit of doing that versus the people that see every big green or red candle and then allow the market to jerk them around.

03:36.060 --> 03:41.820
Meanwhile, over in TLT, which I am still terming the most contrarian trade that I know of at the moment.

03:41.960 --> 03:43.640
